Spore Card — a PNG card that is a seed, and the mesh that only accepts what it can reproduce.
Powered by the Konomi architecture, created by Thomas Frumkin.

Vendored, credited:
- spore.mjs, organ.mjs        — sjgant80-hub/fall-spore (MIT): the seed format and germination engine.
                                 PATCHED here (2026-10-12): decodeSpore refuses a fixed genome whose packed setting
                                 points past the end of its grid (found by adversarial review; one such seed made a
                                 re-run take ~125 s). The same fix belongs upstream in fall-spore.
- png.mjs                     — sjgant80-hub/fallkard-forge (MIT): PNG chunk primitives (lossless layer).
- vendor/fall-os/webrtc.mjs   — sjgant80-hub/fall-os (MIT): the hand-pasted-invite WebRTC link (no signalling server).
- vendor/fall-federate/signaling.mjs — sjgant80-hub/fall-federate (MIT): the witness-gated invite envelope check.
- .witness/witness.mjs        — the mutation gate engine (sjgant80-hub/witness, MIT), vendored and credited.

The edge re-run is the-doubt's primitive ("a thing cannot validate itself"), after Gary W. Floyd's GEP
(Guided Entropy Principle), Lumiea Systems / ThunderStruck Service LLC.

Bundled data:
- data/online_shoppers_intention.csv — UCI "Online Shoppers Purchasing Intention Dataset".
  Used to reproduce the sealed held-out AUC locally when a card is grown, and to re-run a received claim.

The NEW code in this repo: spore-card.mjs (the card codec, v1 + v2), envelope.mjs (the signed envelope),
edge.mjs (the edge verdict), mesh.mjs (the two moves), node-tools.mjs / mesh-node.mjs (Node and browser tools),
spore-card-wire.mjs and the pages.
